#{[17592186311213 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186309413 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311213 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311213 #edb/ref 1077 "field-2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311213 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186309413 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311213 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "93f3390e-533a-5d25-83c0-c5daa77f3ccf" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311226 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186308836 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311226 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311226 #edb/ref 1077 "field-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311226 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186308836 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311226 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "95d0ab30-64b1-59c5-b1be-e3cbd8256de2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311234 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186308987 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311234 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186309139 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311234 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186309470 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311234 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186309649 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311234 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186309690 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311234 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311234 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311234 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186309649 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311234 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "9756b53b-26a7-53d0-942d-24a3a520cea9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311349 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186309583 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311349 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186310049 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311349 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186310083 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311349 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186310216 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311349 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186310419 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311349 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311349 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311349 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186310083 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311349 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "c0d80fa9-92b4-56ea-bacd-670e1a568b19" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311665 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186311349 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311665 #edb/ref 1069 "q-336213" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311665 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311665 #edb/ref 1071 "Find a Cartesian equation of the plane that passes through the point $P(2,1,0)$ and is perpendicular to the line \n${\\begin{aligned}x=1 \\\\ y=-2+4t \\\\ z=3+t\\end{aligned}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311665 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "69ff4417-28a7-50ac-aae7-8483ea57f4a8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311665 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we note that the position vector of $P$ is $p=⟨2,1,0⟩.$ From the parametrical equation, we find that the line is parallel to the vector $⟨0,4,1⟩.$ So, the normal vector of the plane is \n\n$$\nn=⟨0,4,1⟩.\n$$\n\nUsing the dot product, we can find the equation of the plane as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨0,4,1⟩ & =⟨2,1,0⟩\\cdot ⟨0,4,1⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨0,4,1⟩ & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to obtain the Cartesian equation of the plane, we substitute $r=⟨x,y,z⟩$ into the equation above. Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨0,4,1⟩ & =4 \\\\ 4y+z & =4 \\\\ 4y+z-4 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311722 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186311234 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311722 #edb/ref 1069 "q-33655" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311722 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311722 #edb/ref 1071 "What is the unit tangent vector to the curve $r(t)=⟨{t}^{4},\\,{t}^{2},\\,4t⟩$ at the point $P(1,1,4)?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311722 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e09c97e7-cdca-5648-a0b0-ca6d528dfc46" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311722 #edb/ref 1074 "For a curve $r(t)=⟨x(t),y(t),z(t)⟩$, the unit tangent vector $T(t)$ at the point $P(x(t),y(t),z(t))$ is given by\n\n$$\nT(t)=\\frac{{r}^{′}(t)}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the value of $t$ that corresponds to the point $P(1,1,4)$ on the given curve. We know that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =⟨1,\\,1,\\,4⟩ \\\\ ⟨{t}^{4},\\,{t}^{2},\\,4t⟩ & =⟨1,\\,1,\\,4⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the respective components gives the system\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}{t}^{4}=1 \\\\ {t}^{2}=1 \\\\ 4t=4.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the third equality, we get $t=1.$ This value satisfies the other two equations. Therefore, the point $P(1,1,4)$ is at the tip of $r(1).$  \n\nNow, we calculate ${r}^{′}(t)$ and evaluate it at $t=1:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{4}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4{t}^{3},\\,2t,\\,4⟩ \\\\ {r}^{′}(1) & =⟨4(1)^{3},\\,2(1),\\,4⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4,\\,2,\\,4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we calculate the magnitude of ${r}^{′}(1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}^{′}(1)‖ & =\\sqrt{{4}^{2}+{2}^{2}+{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{36} \\\\  & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we normalize ${r}^{′}(1)$ and obtain the unit tangent vector to the given curve at $P(1,1,4):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(1) & =\\frac{{r}^{′}(1)}{‖{r}^{′}(1)‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}⟨4,\\,2,\\,4⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{2}{3},\\,\\frac{1}{3},\\,\\frac{2}{3}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311959 #edb/ref 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}]" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311959 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311959 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "0016720f-74fa-55b6-bf01-800b13e638e0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186312039 #edb/ref 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -10\\end{aligned}]" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186312039 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 175921860454